<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/ACL> dcterms:title "ACL" ;
	linkml:description "The ACL method modifies the access control list of the specified resource." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/AMBER%20STRICT> dcterms:title "TLP:AMBER+STRICT" ;
	linkml:description "TLP:AMBER is for limited disclosure, recipients can only spread this on a need-to-know basis within their organization and its clients. Note that TLP:AMBER+STRICT restricts sharing to the organization only. Sources may use TLP:AMBER when information requires support to be effectively acted upon, yet carries risk to privacy, reputation, or operations if shared outside of the organizations involved. Recipients may share TLP:AMBER information with members of their own organization and its clients, but only on a need-to-know basis to protect their organization and its clients and prevent further harm. Note: if the source wants to restrict sharing to the organization only, they must specify TLP:AMBER+STRICT." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/AMBER> dcterms:title "TLP:AMBER" ;
	linkml:description "TLP:AMBER is for limited disclosure, recipients can only spread this on a need-to-know basis within their organization and its clients. Note that TLP:AMBER+STRICT restricts sharing to the organization only. Sources may use TLP:AMBER when information requires support to be effectively acted upon, yet carries risk to privacy, reputation, or operations if shared outside of the organizations involved. Recipients may share TLP:AMBER information with members of their own organization and its clients, but only on a need-to-know basis to protect their organization and its clients and prevent further harm. Note: if the source wants to restrict sharing to the organization only, they must specify TLP:AMBER+STRICT." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/BASELINE-CONTROL> dcterms:title "Baseline Control" ;
	linkml:description "The BASELINE-CONTROL method places the specified collection resource under baseline control." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/BIND> dcterms:title "Bind" ;
	linkml:description "The BIND method adds a binding to the specified collection resource." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/Base> dcterms:title "Base" .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/CHECKIN> dcterms:title "Check In" ;
	linkml:description "The CHECKIN method creates a new version from a checked-out version-controlled resource." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/CHECKOUT> dcterms:title "Check Out" ;
	linkml:description "The CHECKOUT method prepares a version-controlled resource for modification." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/CLEAR> dcterms:title "TLP:CLEAR" ;
	linkml:description "TLP:CLEAR denotes that recipients can spread this to the world, there is no limit on disclosure. Sources may use TLP:CLEAR when information carries minimal or no foreseeable risk of misuse, in accordance with applicable rules and procedures for public release. Subject to standard copyright rules, TLP:CLEAR information may be shared without restriction." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/CONNECT> dcterms:title "Connect" ;
	linkml:description "The CONNECT method establishes a tunnel to the server identified by the target resource." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/COPY> dcterms:title "Copy" ;
	linkml:description "The COPY method duplicates the specified resource." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/DELETE> dcterms:title "Delete" ;
	linkml:description "The DELETE method deletes the specified resource." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/Environmental> dcterms:title "Environmental" .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/GET> dcterms:title "Get" ;
	linkml:description "The GET method requests a representation of the specified resource. Requests using GET should only retrieve data." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/GREEN> dcterms:title "TLP:GREEN" ;
	linkml:description "TLP:GREEN is for limited disclosure, recipients can spread this within their community. Sources may use TLP:GREEN when information is useful to increase awareness within their wider community. Recipients may share TLP:GREEN information with peers and partner organizations within their community, but not via publicly accessible channels. TLP:GREEN information may not be shared outside of the community. Note: when “community” is not defined, assume the cybersecurity/defense community." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/HEAD> dcterms:title "Head" ;
	linkml:description "The HEAD method asks for a response identical to a GET request, but without the response body." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/LABEL> dcterms:title "Label" ;
	linkml:description "The LABEL method adds, sets, or removes labels on a version-controlled resource." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/LINK> dcterms:title "Link" ;
	linkml:description "The LINK method establishes one or more links between resources." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/LOCK> dcterms:title "Lock" ;
	linkml:description "The LOCK method acquires or refreshes a lock on the specified resource." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/MERGE> dcterms:title "Merge" ;
	linkml:description "The MERGE method merges changes from another resource into the specified resource." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/MKACTIVITY> dcterms:title "Make Activity" ;
	linkml:description "The MKACTIVITY method creates a new activity resource." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/MKCALENDAR> dcterms:title "Make Calendar" ;
	linkml:description "The MKCALENDAR method creates a new calendar collection resource." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/MKCOL> dcterms:title "Make Collection" ;
	linkml:description "The MKCOL method creates a new collection resource." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/MKREDIRECTREF> dcterms:title "Make Redirect Reference" ;
	linkml:description "The MKREDIRECTREF method creates a new redirect reference resource." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/MKWORKSPACE> dcterms:title "Make Workspace" ;
	linkml:description "The MKWORKSPACE method creates a new workspace resource." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/MOVE> dcterms:title "Move" ;
	linkml:description "The MOVE method atomically duplicates and deletes the specified resource." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OPTIONS> dcterms:title "Options" ;
	linkml:description "The OPTIONS method describes the communication options for the target resource." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/ORDERPATCH> dcterms:title "Order Patch" ;
	linkml:description "The ORDERPATCH method changes the ordering of members in an ordered collection." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult> dcterms:title "Access Analysis Result" ;
	a linkml:ClassDefinition ;
	skos:exactMatch "ocsf:OcsfAccessAnalysisResult"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/ocsf_objects"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n6108 ;
	linkml:class_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "The Access Analysis Result object describes access relationships and pathways between identities, resources, focusing on who can access what and through which mechanisms. This evaluates access levels (read/write/admin), access types (direct, cross-account, public, federated), and the conditions under which access is granted. Use this for resource-centric security assessments such as external access discovery, public exposure analysis, etc." ;
	linkml:instantiates "ocsf:OcsfFacts"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:is_a <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfObjectBase> ;
	linkml:slot_usage _:c14n1045 ;
	linkml:slots <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult_access_level> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult_access_type> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult_accessors> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult_additional_restrictions> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult_condition_keys> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult_granted_privileges> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult_access_level> dcterms:title "Access Level" ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/ocsf_core"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/access_level"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "access_level" ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/access_level"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "The generalized access level or permission scope granted to the identity through the analyzed policy configuration. Common examples include Read, Write, List, Delete, Admin, or custom permission levels." ;
	linkml:domain <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult> ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult> ;
	linkml:is_a <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/access_level> ;
	linkml:is_usage_slot true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/ocsf_string_t> ;
	linkml:recommended true ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/access_level"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:usage_slot_name "access_level" .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult_access_type> dcterms:title "Access Type" ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/ocsf_core"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/access_type"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "access_type" ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/access_type"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "The type or category of access being granted to the identity. This describes the nature of the access relationship, such as cross-account access, public access, federated access, or third-party integration access. Examples include 'Cross-Account', 'Public', 'Federated', 'Service-to-Service', etc." ;
	linkml:domain <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult> ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult> ;
	linkml:is_a <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/access_type> ;
	linkml:is_usage_slot true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/ocsf_string_t> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/access_type"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:usage_slot_name "access_type" .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult_accessors> dcterms:title "Accessors" ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/ocsf_objects"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/accessors"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "accessors" ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/accessors"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "The identities that are granted access through the analyzed policy configuration. This identifies the specific entity that can exercise the permissions and helps assess the access relationship and potential security implications. Examples include user accounts, service principals, roles, account identifiers, or system identities." ;
	linkml:domain <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult> ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult> ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:is_a <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/accessors> ;
	linkml:is_usage_slot true ;
	linkml:multivalued true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfUser> ;
	linkml:required true ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/accessors"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:usage_slot_name "accessors" .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult_additional_restrictions> dcterms:title "Additional Restrictions" ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/ocsf_objects"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/additional_restrictions"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "additional_restrictions" ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/additional_restrictions"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "Details about supplementary restrictions and guardrails that may limit the granted access, applied through additional policy types such as Resource Control Policies (RCPs) and Service Control Policies (SCPs) in AWS, or other policy constraints." ;
	linkml:domain <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult> ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult> ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:is_a <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/additional_restrictions> ;
	linkml:is_usage_slot true ;
	linkml:multivalued true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAdditionalRestriction> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/additional_restrictions"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:usage_slot_name "additional_restrictions" .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult_condition_keys> dcterms:title "Condition Keys" ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/ocsf_objects"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/condition_keys"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "condition_keys" ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/condition_keys"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "The condition keys and their values that constrain when and how the granted access can be exercised. These conditions define the circumstances under which the access relationship is valid and the privileges can be used. Examples: IP address restrictions like 'aws:SourceIp:192.0.2.0/24', time-based constraints like 'aws:RequestedRegion:us-east-1', MFA requirements like 'aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent:true', or custom conditions based on resource tags and request context." ;
	linkml:domain <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult> ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult> ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:is_a <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/condition_keys> ;
	linkml:is_usage_slot true ;
	linkml:multivalued true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfKeyValueObject> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/condition_keys"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:usage_slot_name "condition_keys" .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult_granted_privileges> dcterms:title "Granted Privileges" ;
	a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/ocsf_core"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/granted_privileges"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "granted_privileges" ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/granted_privileges"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "The specific privileges, actions, or permissions that are granted through the analyzed access relationship. This includes the actual operations that the accessor can perform on the target resource. Examples: AWS actions like 'sts:AssumeRole', 's3:GetObject', 'ec2:DescribeInstances'; Azure actions like 'Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/read'; or GCP permissions like 'storage.objects.get'." ;
	linkml:domain <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult> ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult> ;
	linkml:is_a <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/granted_privileges> ;
	linkml:is_usage_slot true ;
	linkml:multivalued true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccessAnalysisResult> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/ocsf_string_t> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/granted_privileges"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:usage_slot_name "granted_privileges" .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccount> dcterms:title "Account" ;
	a linkml:ClassDefinition ;
	rdfs:seeAlso "https://d3fend.mitre.org/dao/artifact/d3f:CloudUserAccount/"^^xsd:anyURI , "https://d3fend.mitre.org/dao/artifact/d3f:UserAccount/"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:exactMatch "ocsf:OcsfAccount"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/ocsf_objects"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:relatedMatch "d3f:CloudUserAccount"^^xsd:anyURI , "d3f:UserAccount"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n2605 , _:c14n4726 ;
	linkml:any_of _:c14n4266 , _:c14n4722 ;
	linkml:class_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccount"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccount"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "The Account object contains details about the account that initiated or performed a specific activity within a system or application. Additionally, the Account object refers to logical Cloud and Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) based containers such as AWS Accounts, Azure Subscriptions, Oracle Cloud Compartments, Google Cloud Projects, and otherwise." ;
	linkml:instantiates "ocsf:OcsfFacts"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:is_a <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfEntity> ;
	linkml:slot_usage _:c14n6096 ;
	linkml:slots <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccount_is_disabled> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccount_is_locked> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccount_labels> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccount_name> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccount_tags> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccount_type> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccount_type_id> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccount_uid> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfEntity_uid_numeric> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/is_on_premises_sync_enabled> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccountChange> dcterms:title "Account Change" ;
	OIO:inSubset <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/ocsf_category_iam> ;
	a linkml:ClassDefinition ;
	skos:exactMatch "ocsf:OcsfAccountChange"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/ocsf_events_iam"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:relatedMatch "d3f:UserAccountEvent"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n1556 , _:c14n5056 , _:c14n590 , _:c14n6265 , _:c14n813 ;
	linkml:class_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccountChange"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfAccountChange"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:deprecated "Use the <code>user_management</code> class instead." ;
	linkml:description "Account Change events report when specific user account management tasks are performed, such as a user/role being created or role assigned, changed, deleted, renamed, disabled, enabled, locked out or unlocked." ;
	linkml:instantiates "ocsf:OcsfFacts"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:is_a <https://w3id.org/lmodel/ocsf/OcsfIamEvent> ;
